00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.150
which we talked about in our last video

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:21.190
on "Attack On Titan",

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:22.930
but then after double crossing Zeke,

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:24.950
Erengets the power of the founding Titan

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.930
and goes all out to destroy
everyone on the planet

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.920
who isn't on Paradis Island.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.350
While Eren is really going for it now.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.170
Some of our friends and
enemies are working together

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:39.800
in a last ditch effort to stop
him from doing a genocide.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.680
And then so much is Eren and the Yeagers,

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.870
and of course the Marleyans

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.760
are fueled by negative of emotions,

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.048
our gang of potential heroes has a chance

00:02:47.048 --> 00:02:50.000
only if they stop relying on feelings,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.530
and instead try to do something positive

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:56.000
by working towards some
genuinely good principles.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.210
And how do they do this?

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.000
A little bit of good old fashion stoicism.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.260
So what is stoicism?

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.780
Usually, if someone is described as stoic,

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.180
it's like when you're
talking about an old man

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.620
with no feelings who drinks
whiskey for breakfast

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.960
and is unexpectedly always chopping wood

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.800
and putting it into
neatly organized piles.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.480
And while that dude obviously rips,

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.800
this is not quite

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.520
with the original stoic
we're talking about.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.560
In a general sense, they were descendants

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.360
in the line of virtue ethics.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.160
A school of thought that began with Plato

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.040
and really found its legs with Aristotle.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.020
If you're unfamiliar with the concept,

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.640
Aristotle said that living a virtuous life

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:37.080
was all about orienting
your life towards happiness.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.540
Now he used the term
Telos which means aim,

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.180
to describe the way in which a virtue

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.840
gives us an aim for our activity.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.010
When he says happiness,

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:48.590
he's not referring to a
general feeling of contentment

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:51.730
or swimming in good
vibes and great oldies.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.570
Instead, he's talking about eudaimonia,

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:55.810
which is a type of happiness

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.860
that has to do with human flourishing,

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:01.820
i.e. living your absolute best life.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:04.590
The Stoics turned this idea of virtue

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.140
into a full on philosophy of life.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.870
And it wasn't really
focused on heady concepts

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.520
or metaphysical ponds,

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.320
but about actual human existence.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.640
Would've thought,

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:19.030
a philosophy that's just
about living your actual life.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.080
Now for the Stoics,
the point of philosophy

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.561
was basically being good at life.

00:04:23.561 --> 00:04:25.526
As Pierre Hadot describes it,

00:04:25.526 --> 00:04:27.400
for the stoic then,

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.340
doing philosophy meant
practicing how to live.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:32.960
That is, how to live
freely and consciously.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.530
Consciously, in that we
pass beyond the limits

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:38.290
of individuality to recognize ourselves

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:41.290
as a part of the reason-animated Cosmos.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:43.360
Freely, and that we give up desiring

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:46.530
that which does not depend on
us and is beyond our control

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:49.570
so as to attach ourselves
only to what depends on us,

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:52.900
actions which are just in
conformity with reason.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:53.733
Okay.

00:04:53.733 --> 00:04:56.321
Enough about long dead Greek dudes,

00:04:56.321 --> 00:04:58.700
let's check out what happens

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:03.014
when emotions kind of
tear Zeke and Eren apart.

00:05:03.014 --> 00:05:07.681
- [Zeke] (speaking in foreign language)

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:19.724
- [Eren] (speaking in foreign language)

00:05:19.724 --> 00:05:21.053
- [Zeke] Eren...

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:26.053
- [Eren] (speaking in foreign language)

00:05:26.433 --> 00:05:27.516
- I didn't see this coming.

00:05:27.516 --> 00:05:32.486
- [Eren] (speaking in foreign language)

00:05:32.486 --> 00:05:33.319
- That Sucks.

00:05:33.319 --> 00:05:34.720
You know, you find your long lost brother

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:36.600
and think you have someone
you can like love and trust.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.930
Now, obviously this right
here is not stoicism.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:42.530
But it's important to help
us understand stoicism

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.250
the same way that like
watching blood on the asphalt

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:46.800
in Driver's Ed helps you learn

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.580
about not speeding up the lover's lane

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:49.760
without your seatbelt on

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:53.180
and also why necking can
and will get you pregnant.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:55.900
Now, what we just saw is basically
the opposite of stoicism.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:57.050
And Zeke and Eren,

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.930
and of course like
everyone else on the show,

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:01.320
are being driven completely by passion,

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.767
namely anger and hatred,

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:03.970
and for the Stoics,

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:06.450
being virtuous wasn't simply
about orienting your life

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:07.420
around goodness.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.030
It was also about control,

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:11.820
in particular, controlling
your passions and emotions.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:14.980
So if a committed stoic
was driving on the freeway

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.730
after a horrible day at work

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.070
and got cut off by someone

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:20.420
with a baby on board sticker on their car,

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:23.690
they wouldn't be overcome with
the passion to flick them off

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:24.980
with a burning hatred.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.000
Also, babies are bad drivers.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.150
This because stoicism
necessitates controlling passions

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:33.960
and emotions so that when acts
solely unvirtuous principles.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.650
And while giving someone the double birds

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.950
while using your knees
to drive the car is fun,

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.110
it's not virtuous.

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:42.050
What we see in both Zeke and Eren's plans

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.870
and their outcomes is what happens

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:46.210
when one's thoughts and
actions are dictated

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:49.700
by emotion and passion, and
not reason and deliberation.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.690
So let's check out a
really interesting scene

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:55.490
where we flash back to
one of the many scenarios

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:58.279
that seem to be at the
heart of Eren's rage.

00:06:58.279 --> 00:07:02.946
- [Eren] (speaking in foreign language)

00:07:11.762 --> 00:07:14.530
(audience claps)

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.800
- Any political leader
that doesn't do that move,

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:17.820
they're never good.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:18.926
Now here we get a flashback sequence

00:07:18.926 --> 00:07:21.740
that gives us a little bit of insight

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:23.310
into Eren's initial decision

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:26.750
to sow the seeds of his genocide plan.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.170
And it shows us what happens
when a motion takes over.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.040
Now Eren and the Scouts
are visiting Marley

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:33.160
to try ice cream for the first time

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:36.950
and get blitz at a migrant
camp and forge a plan of peace

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:39.050
with the subjects of a
near protection group.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:41.010
However, during this
meeting of the assembly,

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:42.520
the leader of the protection group

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.060
basically goes full Hitler

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:46.450
when he calls for the citizens of Paradis

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:47.970
to be exterminated.

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:51.740
This political fervor is very unstoic

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:55.170
and that it's both fueled
by emotion, namely hatred,

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:57.930
isn't oriented around any type of virtue,

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.410
things like courage,
justice, or moderation,

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.440
and is operating on the assumption

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:06.080
that one group of humans
is fundamentally inferior

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.010
to the other.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:09.180
In contrast, Stoics would recognize

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:12.240
that nature has not given us that memo.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.670
This right here is why logic
was crucial to the Stoics,

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:18.340
and I'm not talking about
the type of formal logic,

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.850
that's the philosophical
equivalent of algebra,

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:24.020
thank God, but a simple
logical deliberation

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:26.130
on whether or not a specific position

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:28.150
or set of actions is virtuous.

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.770
Again, following in the
Aristotelian tradition,

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:33.340
the Stoics consider logical deliberation

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:35.569
to be a crucial part of virtue.

00:08:35.569 --> 00:08:37.610
That's because unbridled emotions

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:39.950
can easily sway one to extremes.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:43.260
While logical consideration
helps us arrive at more moderate

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:45.656
and thus more virtuous positions.

00:08:45.656 --> 00:08:49.012
And here we see the Scouts
come into the assembly,

00:08:49.012 --> 00:08:52.240
hoping to arrive at a logical position.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:54.690
But all they observe is genocidal fervor.

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:57.450
And it seems like this is a
sort of final straw for Eren

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.550
as his response to the Marleyans hatred

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:02.716
is just a much much, much gnarlier hatred

00:09:02.716 --> 00:09:04.820
aimed back at them.

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:07.000
Now, another important aspect of stoicism

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.444
is that even when you're not
doing xenophobia for lulls,

00:09:10.444 --> 00:09:13.650
living a good life isn't
just about seeking out things

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.370
that are pleasurable for you.

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:17.280
Things like wealth, health comfort,

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.920
and is this toilet paper or cake?

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.350
And in the wake of Eren's victory,

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:25.460
Jean is put in a position to
weigh his individual comfort

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.871
versus virtuous principles.

00:09:27.871 --> 00:09:30.499
So let's check that out real quick.

00:09:30.499 --> 00:09:34.661
- [Jean] (speaking in foreign language)

00:09:34.661 --> 00:09:35.807
- I wanna come to your life.

00:09:35.807 --> 00:09:38.066
- [Man] (speaking in foreign language)

00:09:38.066 --> 00:09:40.356
- [Jean] (speaking in foreign language)

00:09:40.356 --> 00:09:44.939
- [Man] (speaking in foreign language)

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:54.490
- Now here, Jean is tempted
by the opportunity to retire

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:57.370
and live a good life as a hero of Paradis.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:58.203
Now, in one sense,

00:09:58.203 --> 00:10:00.799
it might seem like
pursuing health and wealth

00:10:00.799 --> 00:10:02.320
aren't bad things.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:03.426
It might even be virtuous,

00:10:03.426 --> 00:10:06.180
assuming that you're not
overtly hurting anyone

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:07.280
in the process.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:08.840
But according to the Stoics,

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:13.200
something can only truly be
virtuous when it's also just,

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.550
meaning that the ends we pursue

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:17.570
don't make life (beep) for others

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:20.230
or happen at their expense.

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:23.770
Now, Jean could just hang out
and enjoy the spoils of war,

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:27.080
but in doing so, he's
basically going to be sleeping

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:29.343
in a bed built by genocide

00:10:29.343 --> 00:10:31.900
which tend to have really scratchy sheets

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.230
that are soaked with tears
of anguish and despair.

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:36.570
Now, we see in the wake of Eren's plan,

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.920
that flock and the Yeagers got drunk

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:40.230
with power pretty quickly.

00:10:40.230 --> 00:10:42.830
But those like Jean who are able to leave,

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.030
are operating more in line with stoicism,

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:46.460
as they're pursuing virtues,

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:48.780
like justice, courage and moderation

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.170
above pursuing power and wealth.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.003
Okay.

00:10:52.003 --> 00:10:53.793
Speaking of being virtuous,

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:58.243
what would the stoics think
